      "writtenOn": "2020-10-12T09:51:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we even need this at all ?\n\nIIUC the point of doing this is to tear down the VPN when the interface goes down. mObserver is an instance of BaseNetworkObserver and it is registered with netd in line 420. I\u0027m not very familiar with the netd network observers, but ISTM this should be enough to receive all events about the interface ; if you look at the implementation of mObserver you\u0027ll see that it does nothing if there is no legacy runner, and it will actually call exitIfOuterInterfaceIs() with the name of the interface.\n\nSo I think this callback (and the older broadcast receiver) is not even needed any more. If you find that for some reason netd doesn\u0027t call this when the interface goes down, then it\u0027s the other way around : you should remove the observer and only call exitVpnRunner directly here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2734,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 2734,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "df7f4a3ab57d83ff35a170404882c31fab8db9e1",
